    "background_story": "Dilan was a brilliant and ambitious geologist who had always been fascinated by the mysteries of the earth's crust. His latest obsession was the study of petrous rocks, particularly those found in the rugged mountains of his native country. Dilan spent years researching and collecting samples, often venturing into treacherous terrain to uncover the secrets of these ancient stones. His tireless efforts paid off when he discovered a rare and valuable deposit of petrous rock, which he named 'Dilanite' in honor of his family. The find made him an overnight sensation in the scientific community, and he was hailed as a leading expert in his field. Dilan's love for petrous rocks had not only brought him success but also a deeper appreciation for the natural world and its many wonders.",
